    "notes": "1. Total Revenue is constructed as the sum of all revenue line items, including Interest Income and Interest Expense (which is a negative component). This follows the bank's presentation where 'Total net revenue' = Noninterest revenue + Net interest income. Net interest income = Interest income - Interest expense. Therefore, to reconstruct total revenue from components, we list Interest Income and Interest Expense separately, with Interest Expense as a negative number.\n2. Total Operating Cost includes all operating expenses that reduce income. For a bank, this includes Provision for credit losses and all Noninterest expense components (Compensation, Occupancy, Technology, Professional services, Marketing, Other expense). These are all positive numbers as they reduce income.\n3. Taxes and Interest Expenses are reported as positive numbers as they are costs that reduce income, per the sign convention rule.\n4. All numbers are taken directly from the primary consolidated income statement on Page 205. Supplementary tables provide breakdowns but do not alter the totals used here.\n5. Scale is 1,000,000 (millions) as indicated in the statement.\n6. Currency is USD.",
